Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probes target masked BERT4Rec through a compatibility view; backbone 
implementation details are not supplied. Relevant interfaces are `item_emb`, 
`log2feats(sequence)`, and `predict_score(features, items)`. For user geometry, 
training histories are truncated, LEFT-padded, and given an appended reserved 
MASK token. The user representation is the feature at the maximum nonpadding 
index—the appended MASK position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
alongside training histories and metadata references. It resolves the model’s 
`sample_batch` function to obtain corruption bookkeeping when available.

The margin probe consumes up to ten `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` 
batches with matching B × L shapes. It validates token ranges, computes sequence
features, and scores stacked positive/negative items, requiring B × L × 2 
logits. Feature probes run in evaluation mode without gradients and restore the 
previous training mode.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Directional alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings, excluding
padding/MASK, and maps mean pairwise cosine to [0,1]. Higher values indicate 
stronger alignment, not conclusive collapse.
- **Representation geometry:** Samples up to 256 items and users; reports raw 
norms, centered variance, singular values, and RankMe effective rank. Very low 
variance/rank can flag limited representation spread; larger values alone do not
establish recommendation quality.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Reports mean, tenth percentile, negative-win 
rate, and fraction below 0.5 over valid supervised positions. Larger margins and
lower failure rates indicate clearer sampled-item separation.
- **Coverage and allocation:** Counts valid targets, terminal targets, observed 
input types, and empty batches. Exact corruption branches are counted only when 
sampler bookkeeping matches all batch arrays. Optional training allocation 
counters describe measured branch participation and loss accounting; they are 
distinct from diagnostic coverage.

# Perturbation & Tests

The geometry probe constructs appended-MASK histories. The margin probe observes
supplied corrupted training inputs; it does not independently perturb sequences,
compare counterfactual predictions, or test order sensitivity.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, containing 
geometry, alignment, allocation, margin summaries, and coverage breakdowns. 
Unavailable measurements are null; category lists remain empty because item 
categories are unavailable.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds these measurements and definitions into a 
prompt requesting status, findings, implications, and evidence. These training 
probes do not measure host validation HR@10, recommendation diversity, simulator
traits, or generalization.

