Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
BERT4Rec combines scaled item embeddings with absolute position embeddings, 
dropout, a bidirectional Transformer encoder with padding-key masking, and final
normalization. Serving left-pads history, retains at most `maxlen−1` items, and 
appends reserved MASK. The final MASK representation produces candidate logits. 
Residual patching specifically requires two pre-norm encoder layers.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the trained network through 
`view.model`, plus `item_emb`, `log2feats`, `predict_score`, training histories,
metadata, and category identity. The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive,
negative)` with matching B×L tensors. Diagnosis runs in evaluation mode without 
gradients and restores model mode and random states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings, excluding 
PAD/MASK, and maps mean off-diagonal cosine to [0,1]. High values indicate 
alignment; 0.5 means approximately zero mean cosine, without establishing 
representation quality.
- **Masked-target separation:** Checks reserved tokens and all-MASK supervision 
across at most ten batches. Reports positive-minus-negative mean, 10th 
percentile, negative-win rate, and margins below 0.5. Larger margins and fewer 
negative wins indicate stronger in-sample separation.
- **Serving parity:** Reloads the current category checkpoint, verifies exact 
state identity, and compares explicit, ModelView, internal, exported, and 
batched scoring. Passing requires finite matching scores, identical rankings, 
and complete length/batching coverage.

# Perturbation & Tests
After sampler and parity checks pass, up to 64 seeded training users provide one
eligible prefix each, evaluated against its target and 99 unique unseen 
negatives. Tests delete equally many recent or older items into PAD holes or 
swap the last two items, preserving positions and candidates. Outputs include 
score/rank/reciprocal-rank/hit deltas, ranking overlap, and paired-user 
bootstrap intervals.

A nominal 30-second residual pilot replaces the latest history item and patches 
input or intermediate residuals. Exploration locks sites/signs; disjoint 
confirmation users support sign tests. Identity, structural-zero, 
MASK-restoration, unrelated-donor, and norm-matched random controls assess 
implementation and intervention specificity.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
Returns `{"metrics": ..., "metric_definitions": ...}` with status, availability,
counts, parity, sensitivity, patch records/summaries, uncertainty, and elapsed 
time. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` requests evidence-linked JSON 
interpretation.

These are training-prefix diagnostics, not host validation results. 
Single-category output cannot establish four-category macro effects or global 
Holm discoveries. Missing values mean unavailable. Optimization trajectories, 
semantic donor compatibility, hidden traits, and unavailable review/item 
attributes remain unassessed; sensitivity does not establish recommendation 
quality or successful repairs.

