Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probes target masked BERT4Rec through a compatibility view; backbone 
implementation is not supplied. Relevant hooks are real-item embeddings, 
per-position sequence features, and candidate logits. User representations use 
left-padded histories truncated to `maxlen - 1`, followed by a reserved MASK 
token. Readout selects the maximum nonpadding index, correctly handling left 
padding.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual module through `view.model`, 
plus `item_emb`, `log2feats`, `predict_score`, histories, and metadata handles. 
It resolves the model’s `sample_batch` function for optional corruption 
bookkeeping.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with matching B × L 
tensors. Up to ten batches are checked for valid shapes and token ranges. 
Features and paired candidate IDs produce B × L × 2 logits. Forward probes run 
without gradients in evaluation mode and restore the previous training mode.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Directional alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings with seed 
42, averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result to [0,1]. 
Higher values indicate stronger alignment, not proven collapse.
- **Representation geometry:** Separately samples up to 256 items and users. 
Reports raw norms, centered variance, centered singular values, and RankMe 
effective rank. Low variance/rank can suggest restricted representations; no 
universal healthy threshold is supplied.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Measures mean and lower-decile logit 
margins, negative-win frequency, and margins below 0.5. Larger margins and lower
failure rates indicate stronger sampled separation.
- **Coverage and allocation:** Counts valid targets, final-position targets, 
observed input types, and empty batches. Corruption branches are counted only 
when all batch arrays exactly match sampler bookkeeping. Optional training 
allocation counters are exposed separately.

# Perturbation & Tests

The module constructs appended-MASK inference contexts and inspects 
loader-provided corruptions. It does not perform controlled history 
perturbations or compare predictions before and after edits.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
nested geometry, coverage, and allocation data. Unavailable measurements use 
null; category lists remain empty because item categories are unavailable.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both dictionaries and requests JSON 
containing `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`.

These probes do not measure host validation HR@10, recommendation diversity, 
causal sensitivity, or simulator traits. Diagnostic coverage cannot establish 
training branch allocation; coefficient shares do not establish gradient shares.

