Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe targets masked BERT4Rec through a ModelView wrapper; the backbone 
implementation is not supplied. Relevant hooks are real-item embeddings, 
per-position sequence features, and candidate logits. User representations are 
computed from left-padded training histories, truncated to reserve space for an 
appended MASK. Readout selects the maximum nonpadding index, correctly handling 
left padding.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual module through `view.model`, 
plus `item_emb`, `user_train`, `meta_data`, and `review_data`. It discovers 
`sample_batch` from the module’s defining Python module.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with matching B × L 
shapes. The probe validates shapes and token ranges, calls 
`log2feats(sequence)`, then scores stacked positive/negative candidates through 
`predict_score`, requiring B × L × 2 logits. Forward probes run in evaluation 
mode without gradients; prior training mode is restored.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding directional alignment:** Mean pairwise cosine over up to 2,048 
sampled real-item embeddings, mapped to [0,1]. Higher values indicate stronger 
alignment, not conclusive collapse.
- **Representation geometry:** Separately samples up to 256 items and users. 
Reports raw mean norm, centered variance, centered singular values, and RankMe 
effective rank. Low variance/rank can indicate restricted representations; 
larger values do not establish better recommendations.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Across up to ten batches, reports mean, tenth 
percentile, negative-beats-positive rate, and fraction below 0.5. Higher margins
and lower error rates indicate clearer sampled-target separation.
- **Coverage and allocation:** Counts supervised input types, terminal targets, 
empty batches, and exactly matched corruption bookkeeping. Separately exposes 
optional runtime training-allocation counters; these describe supervision and 
coefficient allocation, not gradient contributions.

# Perturbation & Tests

There are no controlled sensitivity perturbations or paired comparisons. The 
probe observes sampler-generated MASK/random/unchanged corruption when 
bookkeeping matches exactly. Appended-MASK histories reproduce the inference 
readout convention.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`; unavailable 
measurements are null. Category lists remain empty because item categories are 
unavailable. These training probes do not measure host validation HR@10, 
full-catalog recommendation diversity, causal sensitivity, or simulator traits.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds measured metrics and definitions and 
requests JSON containing `status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and 
`evidence`.

