Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probes target masked BERT4Rec through a compatibility view; the backbone 
implementation is not included. Relevant hooks are `item_emb`, 
`log2feats(sequence)` and `predict_score(features, items)`. User geometry uses 
left-padded training histories truncated to reserve space for an appended MASK. 
It selects the feature at the maximum nonpadding index—the appended MASK 
position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
plus training histories and metadata interfaces. It resolves the model module’s 
`sample_batch` to obtain optional corruption bookkeeping. Diagnostic batches 
contain `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with matching B × L shapes. 
Features and paired positive/negative scores are computed through the view. 
Geometry and margin probes run in evaluation mode without gradients and restore 
the previous mode.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Directional alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings, excluding
padding and MASK. Mean pairwise cosine is mapped to [0,1]. Higher values 
indicate stronger alignment, which alone does not establish collapse.
- **Representation geometry:** Separately samples up to 256 items and users. 
Reports raw norms, centered variance, singular values and entropy-based 
effective rank (RankMe). Small variance or low rank can indicate limited 
representation spread; larger values do not guarantee recommendation quality.
- **Positive/negative margins:** Over at most ten batches, computes positive 
minus negative logits at valid supervised positions. Reports mean, tenth 
percentile, negative-win rate and fraction below 0.5. Higher margins and lower 
failure rates indicate stronger sampled separation.
- **Coverage and allocation:** Counts valid targets, terminal targets, observed 
input types and empty batches. Exact corruption branches require matching 
sampler bookkeeping. Optional runtime training allocation records branch counts 
and loss contributions; these are not gradient shares.

# Perturbation & Tests

No explicit shuffle, deletion or counterfactual sensitivity test is implemented.
Probes inspect loader-supplied corruption and construct appended-MASK histories 
for geometry.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`; unavailable 
measurements may be null. Category summaries are explicitly unavailable. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both dictionaries and requests a grounded 
JSON interpretation containing status, findings, implications and evidence.

These training probes do not measure host validation HR@10, full-catalog 
ranking, recommendation diversity or causal effects of training allocation. 
Fixed samples and sampled negatives limit coverage.

