Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis targets a two-layer, pre-norm BERT4Rec: scaled item embeddings plus 
absolute position embeddings pass through dropout, bidirectional Transformer 
layers, and final normalization. Histories are left padded, truncated to 
`maxlen−1`, and followed by a reserved MASK. Its final-slot feature supplies the
user representation for candidate scoring; PAD holes are excluded from attention
keys.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses the actual network through `view.model`,
embeddings through `view.item_emb`, training histories, and 
`log2feats`/`predict_score`. Loader batches contain `(None, sequence, positive, 
negative)` with matching B×L tensors.

Serving verification reloads the current category’s exported checkpoint, checks 
exact state identity, and compares explicit encoder features, ModelView outputs,
internal scoring, exported prediction, and batched versus individual scoring. 
Short, full, and truncated histories must all be covered.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** mapped mean pairwise cosine over up to 2,048 
real-item embeddings. Near 1 indicates strong alignment; 0.5 means approximately
zero mean cosine, without establishing capacity or quality.
- **Masked-target separation:** up to ten batches yield mean/p10 
positive-minus-negative margins, negative-win rate, and margins below 0.5. 
Larger margins and fewer negative wins indicate stronger in-sample separation. 
Sampler checks enforce reserved tokens and MASK-only supervised positions.
- **History sensitivity:** up to 64 seeded training users contribute one 
eligible prefix and 100 fixed candidates. Measurements include target 
score/rank, reciprocal rank, diagnostic hit@10, top-10 overlap, and complete 
ranking agreement. Paired changes receive 500-bootstrap user intervals; 
sensitivity itself is not inherently good or bad.

# Perturbation & Tests

Delete matched counts of recent or older items into PAD holes, preserving 
positions, or swap the final two items. Sensitivity requires passing sampler and
serving checks.

A 30-second residual-patching pilot replaces the latest item using two 
frequency/recency-matched donor rules. Clean/corrupted activations are patched 
before attention layers. Exploration locks sites/signs; disjoint confirmation 
users receive sign tests. Identity, structural-zero, MASK-restoration, 
norm-matched random, and unrelated-donor controls accompany margin/ranking 
effects.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including 
status, counts, availability, parity, sensitivity, patching records, controls, 
intervals, and elapsed time. Execution restores model mode and RNG states.

Null means unavailable. These are training-prefix diagnostics, not host 
validation. Four-category macro results and global Holm adjustment remain 
unavailable locally. Training trajectories, semantic donor compatibility, hidden
labels, unavailable metadata, and simulator traits are unassessed. Patching 
cannot establish repair or validation gains.

