Reflection 1: current report is not sufficient because ['The catalog audit is a 
useful supplementary diagnostic, but it does not answer the starting question: 
whether the fixed 0.5 objective improves host macro validation HR@10 over 
terminal-only and reconstruction-only controls. The report defers those controls
and the paired gradient audit without specifying a replacement decision rule or 
budget allocation. Research progress of 40% does not establish remaining GPU 
budget.', 'The preregistration remains incomplete: exact endpoint sampling, 
branch assignment, reconstruction corruption, loss and negative-sampling 
definitions, frequency/history bins, checkpoint cadence, chunk size, compute 
cap, and uncertainty procedure are unspecified. Equal branch coefficients alone 
do not fix branch exposure or gradient influence.', 'A sampled/full-catalog 
performance gap is expected from nested candidate sets and is not itself 
evidence of a model defect. Conditional on full-catalog target rank and uniform 
sampling without replacement, sampled hit probability can be calculated using a 
hypergeometric distribution. This provides an exact reference and separates 
candidate-sampling variability from user variability.', 'Matching scoring dtype 
does not ensure identical scores across different chunk shapes. Reuse catalog 
scores for sampled candidates, retain the target score once, and compute rank as
one plus the number of competitors ahead under the declared score/item-ID 
ordering. A zero target-minus-tenth-competitor margin requires tie-aware 
interpretation.', 'Training-prefix targets may already have been supervised 
during fitting, and catalog competitors can include later training interactions.
The audit correctly remains in-sample, but its eligibility restrictions also 
limit relevance to repeated-item prediction and future serving. With only 32 
users/category, crossed frequency/history strata may be too sparse for useful 
comparisons.', 'Serving-parity success belongs to a particular supplied run; 
another supplied run fails category identification. Require fresh parity for the
actual audited checkpoint. Originality 4 and potential 7 are optimistic without 
evidence of diagnostic usefulness; difficulty 3 describes chunked scoring better
than complete integration, reproducibility, and failure reporting.'], generating
follow-up queries
